WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.545
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit
1: Family, Identity, and History.

2
00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:07.769
This is Unit 1: Family, Identity, and History.

3
00:00:07.849 --> 00:00:15.268
In this unit, you will explore some of the most important
questions a person can ask: Where do I come from?

4
00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:17.511
Who are the people in my family?

5
00:00:17.591 --> 00:00:21.645
What stories have been passed down through the generations?

6
00:00:21.725 --> 00:00:26.691
You will read about families, learn
how to describe your own background,

7
00:00:26.771 --> 00:00:32.508
and discover how people across East Africa
and the wider world have moved, settled,

8
00:00:32.588 --> 00:00:35.241
and built new lives over the centuries.

9
00:00:35.321 --> 00:00:41.128
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:49.027
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
understand a passage about family history and migration,

11
00:00:49.107 --> 00:00:51.397
and discuss its ideas in English.

12
00:00:51.477 --> 00:00:57.932
You will also use the past simple tense correctly
to describe completed actions and events.

13
00:00:58.012 --> 00:01:03.676
You will also distinguish between the
past simple and the present perfect tense.

14
00:01:03.756 --> 00:01:06.333
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:13.031
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: belligerent,
malevolence, vindictive, infuriate, animosity, narcissistic.

16
00:01:13.111 --> 00:01:17.590
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

17
00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:21.136
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

18
00:01:21.216 --> 00:01:27.959
The reading sequence includes Keeping the Story Alive:
Oral History and Heritage and The Journey of Alina's Family.

19
00:01:28.039 --> 00:01:28.789
Read actively.

20
00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:32.883
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

21
00:01:32.963 --> 00:01:36.739
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

22
00:01:36.819 --> 00:01:40.105
The first language focus is The Past Simple Tense.

23
00:01:40.185 --> 00:01:46.096
The past simple tense describes actions and
events that started and finished in the past,

24
00:01:46.176 --> 00:01:48.721
which makes it the storyteller's tense.

25
00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:54.375
Almost every sentence in a biography, a
family history or a chronicle depends on it,

26
00:01:54.455 --> 00:01:57.808
so this unit treats it as your most important tool.

27
00:01:57.888 --> 00:02:05.145
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

28
00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:09.693
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: Present Your Family Biography.

29
00:02:09.773 --> 00:02:13.868
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

30
00:02:13.948 --> 00:02:17.046
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

31
00:02:17.126 --> 00:02:20.348
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

32
00:02:20.428 --> 00:02:21.941
You are ready to begin.

33
00:02:22.021 --> 00:02:28.799
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

34
00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:32.124
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

35
00:02:32.204 --> 00:02:39.952
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
